        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: American Astronomical Society\n- Awards: Beatrice M. Tinsley Prize\n- People: Beatrice Tinsley\n- Roles: astronomer, cosmologist\n- Topics: astronomy, astrophysics, galaxy evolution\n\nFacts:\n- Beatrice Muriel Hill Tinsley was born on 27 January 1941 and died on 23 March 1981.\n- Beatrice Tinsley was a British-born New Zealand astronomer and cosmologist.\n- Beatrice Tinsley made fundamental research contributions to the astronomical understanding of how galaxies evolve, grow, and die.\n- The American Astronomical Society awards the Beatrice M. Tinsley Prize every other year.\n- The Beatrice M. Tinsley Prize recognizes an outstanding research contribution to astronomy or astrophysics of an exceptionally creative or innovative character.\n- The Beatrice M. Tinsley Prize is named in honor of the cosmologist and astronomer Beatrice Tinsley.",
